{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style syntax-guided reduction)\n\nThe goal is to implement `solve(case)` that:\n1. Takes a parse tree with nodes having id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility fields\n2. Has `required_symbols` that must always remain represented\n3. Reduces the tree by removing nodes bottom-up (deeper nodes first)\n4. A node can only be removed if:\n   - It's marked `removable: true`\n   - It has no retained children\n   - After removal, all required_symbols are still represented by at least one retained node\n5. Tie-breaking at equal depth: use node ID (lexicographic)\n6. Returns `removed_node_ids` (actual removal order) and `retained_node_ids` (sorted)\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes in order: deeper nodes first, ties broken by node ID\n3. For each node in that order:\n   - If removable and no retained children and required symbols still covered after removal → remove it\n   - Otherwise retain it\n4. Return removed (in order processed/removed) and retained (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read:\n- \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" - process deep to shallow\n- \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\"\n- \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\"\n- \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\"\n\nSo the algorithm:\n1. Sort nodes by depth descending, then by node ID ascending (for ties)\n2. Track which nodes are \"retained\" (start with all nodes retained)\n3. For each node in sorted order:\n   - If node.removable is False → keep it (retain)\n   - If node has any children that are currently retained → keep it\n   - If removing would cause any required symbol to have zero representation → keep it\n   - Otherwise → remove it\n4. Return removed_node_ids in the order they were removed, retained_node_ids sorted\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1, parent=root\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2, parent=root\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0, parent=root\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols = [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nSort by depth desc, then id asc:\nDepth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by id: n4, n5, n6)\nDepth 1: n1, n2, n3\nDepth 0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2):\n- removable: yes\n- children of n4: none → no retained children\n- If we remove n4: remaining symbols covered by retained nodes:\n  - root: root → yes\n  - s1: n1 still has symbol s1 → yes\n- Remove n4 ✓\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3):\n- removable: false → retain\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1):\n- removable: yes\n- children of n6: none → no retained children\n- If we remove n6: \n  - root: root → yes\n  - s1: n1 has symbol s1 → yes\n- Remove n6 ✓\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1, parent=root):\n- removable: false → retain\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2, parent=root):\n- removable: yes\n- children of n2: n4 (removed), so no retained children\n- If we remove n2:\n  - root: root → yes\n  - s1: n1 has symbol s1 → yes\n- Remove n2 ✓\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0, parent=root):\n- removable: false → retain\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root, parent=null):\n- removable: false → retain\n\nRemoved: [n4, n6, n2] (in order processed)\nRetained: [root, n1, n3, n5] (sorted)\n\nThat seems reasonable. Now let me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node lookup\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, then by node ID ascending\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    # Track retained set\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    \n    # Track symbol coverage: symbol -\u003e count of retained nodes with that symbol\n    symbol_counts = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not n[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if removing preserves required symbols\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        # If this is the only retained node with this symbol, and it's required\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) \u003c= 1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Remove it\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) - 1\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I need to think about the symbol_counts more carefully. We start with all nodes retained. As we remove nodes, we decrease counts.\n\nActually my logic is correct but let me double-check: `symbol_counts` tracks retained nodes with each symbol. When we check if removing n would break required_symbols: if sym is in required_symbols and symbol_counts[sym] == 1 (this is the last one), we can't remove it.\n\nBut wait, what if sym is not in required_symbols? Then we can always remove regardless of count.\n\nLet me also check if required_symbols validation is needed: \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\"\n\nLet me add validation:\n- All required symbols must be present in at least one node\n- The tree must be valid (parents exist, no cycles, etc.)\n\nActually the spec says \"Validate every required field before computing a result\" and \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\"\n\nLet me add basic validation.\n\nAlso, the \"retained_node_ids\" should be sorted - sorted lexicographically (as strings)? The schema says it's an array of strings. I'll sort lexicographically.\n\nLet me finalize the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    if \"nodes\" not in case or \"required_symbols\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required fields: nodes or required_symbols\")\n    \n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not isinstance(case[\"required_symbols\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a list and required_symbols must be a list\")\n    \n    # Build node lookup\n    node_map = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        for field in (\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"):\n            if field not in n:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing required field: {field}\")\n        node_map[n[\"id\"]] = n\n    \n    # Validate parents exist\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None and n[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {n['id']} references unknown parent {n['parent']}\")\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Validate required symbols are initially present\n    all_symbols = set(n[\"symbol\"] for n in nodes)\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym not in all_symbols:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Required symbol {sym} not present in any node\")\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, then by node ID ascending (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    # Track retained set (initially all nodes)\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    \n    # Track symbol coverage\n    symbol_counts = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not n[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if removing would drop a required symbol to zero\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) \u003c= 1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Remove this node\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Now I need to format it as a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string.\n\nLet me format the output properly. The response must be exactly one JSON object like:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me write the complete Python source and escape it properly.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if \\\"nodes\\\" not in case or \\\"required_symbols\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required fields: nodes or required_symbols\\\")\\n\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols_list = case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(required_symbols_list, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"required_symbols must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    required_symbols = set(required_symbols_list)\\n\\n    # Validate each node has required fields and build lookup\\n    node_map = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        for field in (\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"):\\n            if field not in n:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n        nid = n[\\\"id\\\"]\\n        if nid in node_map:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Duplicate node id: {nid}\\\")\\n        node_map[nid] = n\\n\\n    # Validate parent references\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None and n[\\\"parent\\\"] not in node_map:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {n['id']} references unknown parent {n['parent']}\\\")\\n\\n    # Validate required symbols are present initially\\n    all_symbols = set(n[\\\"symbol\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if sym not in all_symbols:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Required symbol '{sym}' not present in any node\\\")\\n\\n    # Build children map\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Sort: deeper nodes first, ties broken by node ID ascending (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    # Track retained set (initially all nodes retained)\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n\\n    # Track symbol -\u003e count of retained nodes carrying that symbol\\n    symbol_counts = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Node must be explicitly marked removable\\n        if not n[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Node must have no currently-retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Removing must not drop any required symbol to zero coverage\\n        sym = n[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) \u003c= 1:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentative removal passes all checks: commit removal\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) - 1\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_sorted\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01YzIOQP1wuyBLuxHqkK4yYw","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2539},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2539,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":51,"output_tokens":3473,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2615},"service_tier":"standard"}}